          "level": "fallback",
          "summary": "Make PB's at-will termination right unconditional on 30 days' notice and replace the 300% exit multiple with repayment of SFJ's actual funded Development Costs.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We made PB's at-will exit exercisable at any time on thirty (30) days' notice, removing the $60 million funding gate and the pre-first-approval cut-off, and replaced the 300% multiple with repayment of the Development Costs SFJ actually funded. Our position is that the customer may leave on short notice without a penalty; repaying SFJ's funded costs (rather than 3x) is the proportionate landing zone here, and we can discuss a modest capped uplift if SFJ needs a return.",
          "precedentId": "seed-t4c",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0755",
              "oldText": "PB may terminate this Agreement at any time after SFJ has paid or incurred a total of $60 million of Development Costs and prior to the date of receipt of the first Regulatory Approval upon [***] prior written notice to SFJ. In the event that PB terminates this Agreement pursuant to this Section 14.2.2 then in exchange for purchasing the Trial Data Package including the Research Results included therein as set forth in Section 11.1.1.4, PB will pay SFJ, within [***] of the date of termination, an amount equal to three hundred percent (300%) of Development Costs paid or incurred by SFJ prior to such termination.",
              "newText": "PB may terminate this Agreement at any time for convenience, in whole or in part, upon thirty (30) days' prior written notice to SFJ. In the event that PB terminates this Agreement pursuant to this Section 14.2.2 then in exchange for purchasing the Trial Data Package including the Research Results included therein as set forth in Section 11.1.1.4, PB will pay SFJ, within [***] of the date of termination, an amount equal to one hundred percent (100%) of Development Costs paid or incurred by SFJ prior to such termination."
